      "raw": "<p>I&#39;d always been under that impression as well, so the two together allow her to sprint (possibly avoiding the attack) and counterstrike. &nbsp;Normally, only useful against melee attacks, since combat stance resolves second, so the counterstrike wouldn&#39;t have LOS if the shift moved out of LOS of the original attack, but also works against area attacks and external hazard generators, since the attacker and &nbsp;the source of the attack are not the same, so she can sometimes maintain LOS to the former while obstructing it from the latter.</p>",
